Angular CDK provides `cdkTrapFocus` directive for modals. Usage:

```html
<div cdkTrapFocus>
  <!-- modal content -->
</div>
```

For manual focus management, use `@ViewChild` and `ElementRef` with `nativeElement.focus()`. In Angular, avoid direct DOM manipulation; use `Renderer2` for safe interactions.

```typescript
@ViewChild('modalTrigger') trigger: ElementRef;
openModal() {
  this.modalOpen = true;
  setTimeout(() => this.trigger.nativeElement.focus());
}
```

CDK's `LiveAnnouncer` service can announce dynamic content politely or assertively:

```typescript
import { LiveAnnouncer } from '@angular/cdk/a11y';
constructor(private announcer: LiveAnnouncer) {}
this.announcer.announce('Registration successful', 'polite');
```

This creates a hidden live region element and speaks the message. Use it for form submissions, errors, and navigation.
